[SIZE=6][B]Projectile Collision Filter — P-11 Self-Healing & Four Selectable Scopes / 投射物碰撞過濾器[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]English[/B][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cainiao524/HD2-Projectile-Collision-Filter/v0.3.0-preview.8/docs/assets/projectile-collision-filter-cover.png[/IMG]

[SIZE=5][B]Let your P-11 darts heal their owner[/B][/SIZE]

An actual P-11 dart fired by you can hit your own character and trigger native collision and healing. You aim and fire manually; native ammo consumption, fire rate, healing amount and effects remain. No direct health or stamina writing is used.

[B]v0.3.0-preview.8 is a four-choice integrated prerelease.[/B] The user reports normal basic operation with all four choices. Release packaging preserves the tested four Lua payloads and game resources while updating bilingual configuration, copy, tools and artwork. Full per-weapon, host/client, concurrency and performance coverage is still incomplete.

[SIZE=5][B]One Arsenal mod, four scopes[/B][/SIZE]

Configuration is English first, followed by Traditional Chinese. Choose one under [B]Effect Scope / 生效範圍[/B]:

[LIST]
[*][B]P-11 Only / 僅治療手槍[/B]: P-11 healing darts only. Recommended and initially selected.
[*][B]All Sidearms / 手槍全部[/B]: P-11 and supported sidearm projectiles; excludes shotgun and multi-projectile types.
[*][B]All Weapons (No Shotguns) / 全部武器不包括霰彈槍[/B]: P-11 and supported weapon projectiles; excludes shotgun and multi-projectile types.
[*][B]All Weapons (Including Shotguns) / 全部武器包括霰彈槍[/B]: Includes shotgun and multi-projectile types. [B]WARNING: May cause severe performance impact. 警告：可能造成嚴重性能影響。[/B]
[/LIST]

Arsenal controls overall enable/disable. Close the game before changing the scope, then redeploy. Do not manually copy all four resource variants together.

[SIZE=5][B]Performance changes[/B][/SIZE]

One shared core and addon follows the allocation cursor, checking recent projectile candidates with bounded retries instead of the historical repeated traversal of all 2,048 slots. Local ownership, weapon/projectile identity, original-value checks, fresh write guards and readback remain mandatory.

An earlier user report confirmed healing and roughly [B]70 → 130 FPS with P-11 0.2.3[/B]. It was a single older-candidate report without a complete benchmark setup, [B]not a fixed gain for the four preview.8 scopes[/B]. Candidate checks still have a cost; heavy traffic, expired hints or collision timing can cause skipped projectiles. Zero overhead, no stutter and success on every shot are not promised.

